Add the Sky1 system, FCH and AUDSS reset providers with ACPI and
DT support. Validate firmware indices before table access, suppress
unsafe manual provider unbind, make the mandatory AUDSS NOC provider
a Kconfig dependency, and keep AUDSS register accesses inside the
clock supplier runtime-PM lifetime. Retain the exact legacy lookup
API needed by 6.18 and 7.0; 7.1 uses the native fwnode reset path.

Provenance: System, FCH and ACPI reset adaptations derive from
cixtech/cix-linux-main@19f2947303670f2e5734d6a96ffc72a80fd9b942
patches-7.1/0006* (00060-00062 on 7.1). The public
AUDSS binding/reset identifiers also trace to v9
at https://patchwork.kernel.org/series/1124659/. Bounds checks,
dependency corrections, unbind suppression and power/lifetime coupling
are overlay-created remediation.

